(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Handing NDSolve the smooth-noise measurement equation: a monitored particle \
on a grid\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A quantum particle whose position is continuously monitored obeys \
a stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation, and the companion essay in \
this folder showed how to hand such an equation to ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 StyleBox[" for a qubit: write it in Stratonovich form and replace the white \
noise by a smooth interpolated Wiener path. This document carries the same \
trick into continuous space, where the state is a wavefunction on a grid and \
the equation is a stochastic partial differential equation. The route has one \
genuinely new obstacle: the physical equation's coefficients contain ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 StyleBox[", an integral of the unknown, and ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 StyleBox[" cannot discretize an integral of the unknown. The fix is to \
integrate the linear, unnormalized form of the equation, whose coefficients \
are the bare operators ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 StyleBox[" and ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 StyleBox[", and to read the physics through the decaying norm, which is not \
a defect but the likelihood of the record. Every step is certified in place: \
the Stratonovich damping is verified symbolically, the noise-off solver is \
held to the exact free and coherent evolutions, the conditional covariance \
flow is solved in closed form and one noisy trajectory is held to it \
pathwise, its two driven means matched against the same noise path through \
exact gains, the deliberately wrong It\[OHat] damping visibly misses, the \
ensemble rebuilds the Lindblad master equation and the law of total variance, \
one record generated by the split-step engine of the parent essay is filtered \
through ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 StyleBox[" to the same conditional state, and the route then leaves the \
quadratic comfort zone entirely, collapsing a double-well cat with only the \
model-free guards on duty.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: August 12, 2026)", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["\<\
Part I: The Measurement Equation, and the Coefficient NDSolve Cannot Hold\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Recall the equation of motion from the parent essay on measurement in a \
potential. A particle with Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " whose position is monitored continuously and weakly obeys the stochastic \
Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         FractionBox[
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"]}], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "-", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["(",
           FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
          RowBox[{
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
           RowBox[{
            StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
             SpanMaxSize->1], 
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
            StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
             SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
          StyleBox[")",
           FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "2"], 
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
        SqrtBox[
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
           StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "]"}], 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " sets how fast position information arrives and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " is a Wiener increment. The detector's output over the same increment is \
the measurement record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ", the conditional mean position buried in shot noise. The parent essay \
integrates this equation with a hand-built engine: a Bayesian measurement \
update alternating with a split-step Fourier drift. Here we ask a different \
question: can ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " swallow the equation whole, discretizing space itself, the way it does for \
an ordinary partial differential equation?"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Not as written, and the obstacle is worth seeing precisely. ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 "'s method of lines turns a partial differential equation into coupled \
ordinary differential equations by sampling every coefficient at grid points. \
The coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " is not a function of the point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 ": it is an integral of the unknown over the whole line, a single number \
that depends on the entire current solution. In other words, the equation is \
nonlocal in exactly the place a spatial discretizer needs locality. Confirm \
that ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " refuses the nonlocal equation, returning unevaluated while ",
 Cell[BoxData["NIntegrate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " reports that it cannot sample the unknown (the two messages below are the \
refusal, not an accident of ours):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Head", "[", 
   RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"D", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"u", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "==",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"I", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"u", "[", 
             RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", "\n", 
         "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"NIntegrate", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"y", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
               RowBox[{"u", "[", 
                RowBox[{"y", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"y", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"u", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"u", "[", 
         RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"E", "^", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "u", ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0.1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "===",
   " ", "NDSolveValue"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the call comes back untouched, with one complaint from each \
layer: the integral cannot sample the still-symbolic unknown, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " classifies what remains as a kind of equation it does not support. The \
gate is real, and no method option opens it. So if ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " is to integrate this physics, the equation itself must change."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The change is standard in quantum filtering, and it is a simplification, \
not an approximation. Drop the two ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 " subtractions and carry an unnormalized state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         FractionBox[
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"]}], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], "-", 
       RowBox[{
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]}], "]"}], 
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Ket"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Ket"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every coefficient is now a pointwise function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 ", exactly what a spatial discretizer wants, and the equation is linear in \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 ". Two things happened in exchange, and they are the two facts the rest of \
this document leans on. First, the equation is driven by the record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " itself, not by the noise: the linear equation is a filter, a machine that \
eats a record and produces the state consistent with it. We will feed it \
records from two different sources, a plain Wiener path in Parts III through \
V and a record generated by an entirely different integrator in Part VI. \
Second, the state no longer stays normalized, and the norm is not garbage: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {GridBox[{
        {
         TemplateBox[{
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
          "Ket"]}
       },
       GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " is the likelihood of the record that drove it, the probability weight that \
turns averages over plain Wiener paths into averages over physical records. \
In other words, normalization was carrying the statistics all along, and the \
linear form simply makes it visible. The normalized state is recovered at any \
moment as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
     "Ket"], "/", GridBox[{
      {GridBox[{
         {
          TemplateBox[{
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
           "Ket"]}
        },
        GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both facts are one algebraic identity away, so let us certify them before \
trusting them. Averaging the outer product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"\|01d53c", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Ket"], 
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Bra"]}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 " over records that are plain Wiener paths, the It\[OHat] rule gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "+", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 ", and that combination should be the Lindblad master equation of \
unmonitored position measurement, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
     FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "~"], "}"}]}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 ". Verify the identity on a three-point grid with every entry symbolic, the \
Hamiltonian an arbitrary Hermitian matrix and the position operator an \
arbitrary real diagonal:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "lam", ",", " ", "hb", ",", " ", "h11", ",", " ", "h22", ",", " ", "h33", ",",
     " ", "h12", ",", " ", "h13", ",", " ", "h23", ",", " ", "x1", ",", " ", 
    "x2", ",", " ", "x3", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ham", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"h11", ",", " ", "h12", ",", " ", "h13"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "h12", "]"}], ",", " ", "h22", ",", " ", 
          "h23"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "h13", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "h23", "]"}], ",", " ", "h33"}], "}"}]}], 
       "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"xop", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"x1", ",", " ", "x2", ",", " ", "x3"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
       RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"ham", "/", "hb"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"lam", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "xop"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"b", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lam", "]"}], " ", "xop"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"a", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "a", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"b", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "b", "]"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", "==",
         "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ham", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], " ", "-", " ", 
              RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "ham"}]}], ")"}], "/", "hb"}]}], 
          " ", "+", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"lam", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "xop"}], " ",
              "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"xop", " ", ".", " ", "xop", " ", ".", " ", "rho"}], 
                " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"rho", " ", ".", " ", "xop", " ", ".", " ", "xop"}]}],
                ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
           "x1", ",", " ", "x2", ",", " ", "x3", ",", " ", "h11", ",", " ", 
            "h22", ",", " ", "h33"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", 
        "&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{"lam", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{"hb", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the unweighted average of the outer products obeys the Lindblad \
equation, with no likelihood weight in sight: any observable linear in the \
density matrix can be averaged directly from the raw, unnormalized states. \
Taking the trace of the same identity kills the commutator and the dissipator \
termwise, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d53c", "\[DoubleVerticalBar]", 
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Ket"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleVerticalBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 " is conserved: the likelihood weight averages to one for all time, a \
property we will use in Part V as the loudest possible alarm bell, since a \
wrong drift sends this average off exponentially. Where the weight genuinely \
matters is for quantities nonlinear in the conditional state, the spread of \
the conditional mean across trajectories being the example Part V works out."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell["\<\
Part II: The Linear Equation in Stratonovich Form: the Damping Doubles\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " integrates ordinary calculus, so the white noise must become a function. \
The companion qubit essay establishes the recipe: draw a Wiener path on a \
grid, interpolate it into a smooth curve ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ", and hand the solver ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " as an ordinary forcing. The price is a change of stochastic calculus. A \
smooth curve of vanishing correlation time integrates to the Stratonovich \
reading of the equation, not the It\[OHat] one, so the drift we hand ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " must be the Stratonovich drift, with the conversion term already inside."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For this equation the conversion is one line of algebra, because the \
diffusion is linear in the state: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Ket"], ")"}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 ". The It\[OHat]-to-Stratonovich correction subtracts half the derivative of \
the diffusion along itself, and for a linear diffusion that derivative is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " again, so the correction is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " at every grid size, with nothing to expand and nothing to truncate. \
Subtracting it from the It\[OHat] drift doubles the damping:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         FractionBox[
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"]}], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], "-", 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
        SuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]}], "]"}], 
     TemplateBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
      "Ket"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
       "Ket"], "\[SmallCircle]", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, the entire difference between the equation ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " sees and the It\[OHat] equation of Part I is the coefficient of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " in place of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 ". That factor of two is the whole design, so it must not rest on our \
algebra alone. Verify it with the built-in conversion, on a three-point grid \
with the strength and the grid points symbolic: hand ",
 Cell[BoxData["StratonovichProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " the doubled damping and the linear diffusion, convert to the It\[OHat] \
form, and compare against the It\[OHat] drift of Part I:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "p1", ",", " ", "p2", ",", " ", "p3", ",", " ", "a1", ",", " ", "a2", ",", 
    " ", "a3", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", 
     RowBox[{"StratonovichProcess", "[", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "lam"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"x1", "^", "2"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"p1", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "lam"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"x2", "^", "2"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"p2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "lam"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"x3", "^", "2"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"p3", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"List", " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lam", "]"}], " ", "x1", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p1", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lam", "]"}], " ", "x2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lam", "]"}], " ", "x3", " ", 
             RowBox[{"p3", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"p1", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"p2", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"p3", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "     ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"p1", ",", " ", "p2", ",", " ", "p3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"a1", ",", " ", "a2", ",", " ", "a3"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Drift\>\"", "]"}], " ", "==", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"lam", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"x1", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"p1", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"lam", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"x2", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"p2", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"lam", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"x3", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"p3", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The measurement terms are diagonal, so each grid component carries the \
conversion independently and three symbolic points certify the pattern for \
any number of them; the Hamiltonian, being noise-free, passes through the \
conversion untouched. Note what did not need converting: the record itself. \
The relation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " has additive noise, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " means the same thing in both calculi, exactly as the qubit essay found for \
its readout row."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell["\<\
Part III: Encoding: the Grid, the Smooth Noise, and One NDSolve Call\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We now build the machinery, reusing the parent essay's conventions so the \
two documents remain one toolbox. Fix units so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mass", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The grid is the parent essay's: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " points across a box of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["l", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " glued into a ring, with the quantized momenta stored beside the positions \
in the order the discrete Fourier transform uses them:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "grid", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "l_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"l", "/", "n"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "n"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<dx\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "dx"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dx", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hbar", "/", "l"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"RotateLeft", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell["\<\
Carry over the transform pair and the two leakage guards. The box is a ring, \
so probability that reaches the wall wraps to the far side, and the momentum \
ladder has a top rung, so probability that reaches the fastest momenta \
aliases into slow motion; each guard measures how much probability sits in \
the outer tenth of its axis:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "ft", ",", " ", "ift", ",", " ", "outerTenth", ",", " ", "edgeMass", ",", 
    " ", "tailMass"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ft", "[", "psi_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
    RowBox[{"psi", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ift", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", 
    RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"outerTenth", "[", 
    RowBox[{"coord_", ",", " ", "probs_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Pick", "[", 
     RowBox[{"probs", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "coord", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0.9", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "coord", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"edgeMass", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "psi_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"outerTenth", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "psi", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"tailMass", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "psi_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"outerTenth", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ft", "[", "psi", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The initial state is the parent's Gaussian packet, in two forms for the two \
engines it will feed: the grid vector, normalized so its absolute squares sum \
to one (each entry carries a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 ", making expectations plain dot products), and the same packet as a \
continuum function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 " with the integral normalization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1", "/", "4"}]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", "4", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], "0"], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],
 ", which is the form ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 " takes as an initial condition. Writing that continuum normalization once, \
as a helper, means no hand-typed prefactor appears again below:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "gaussian", ",", " ", "packet", ",", " ", "xMean", ",", " ", "xVar"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "x0_", ",", " ", "p0_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], 
   " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "x0"}], ")"}],
          "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "p0", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "/", "hbar"}]}]}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x0_", ",", " ", "p0_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"E", "^", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"x", " ", "-", " ", "x0"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"4", " ", 
            RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"I", " ", "p0", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x", "/", "hbar"}]}]}], ")"}]}], "/", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
         RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "^", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "psi_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "psi", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "psi_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "psi", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "psi"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the noise. Draw independent Gaussian increments with variance the grid \
spacing on a uniform time grid, accumulate them into a Wiener path, and \
interpolate with a cubic, so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 " is a continuous curve and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " an ordinary piecewise-smooth function; this is the companion essay's \
recipe verbatim, and the seed makes every path reproducible:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "wienerPath", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
    RowBox[{"tf_", ",", " ", "dtn_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"knots", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
            RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
              RowBox[{"tf", "/", "dtn"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
        "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Interpolation", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"knots", ",", "\n", "       ", 
            RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
               RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", "\n", "          ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"knots", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"knots", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
                 " ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Length", "[", "knots", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                  "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
          "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"InterpolationOrder", " ", "->", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell["\<\
Visualize one realization of the path and the ordinary function that stands \
in for white noise:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"wf", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2.", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GraphicsRow", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"wf", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{
         "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<smooth Wiener path W(t)\>\""}], ",",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<W\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",",
        "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"wf", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", 
         "    ", 
         RowBox[{
         "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
          " ", "\"\<its derivative W'(t): the smooth noise\>\""}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<W'\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "580"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the path is a continuous random walk and its derivative is \
jagged but genuine, varying on the scale of the drawing grid. That drawing \
step is the physics dial of the whole construction: it fixes the correlation \
time of the smoothed noise, hence which stochastic equation we are actually \
solving, converging to the ideal white-noise equation only as it shrinks; we \
return to it with a sweep in Part V.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One decision remains: how ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " should discretize space. Three findings, each established by running the \
alternative rather than by trusting a manual, pin the choice. First, the \
built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["PeriodicBoundaryCondition"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 " always routes the problem to the finite element discretizer, whatever \
method options accompany it; the finite element route does integrate this \
equation, but two orders of magnitude slower and less accurately than what \
follows, so we reject it on cost. Second, on a periodic problem the classic \
idiom is to state periodicity as an equation, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["l", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ",", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["u", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["l", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ",", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 ", which keeps the fast tensor-product grid available. Third, on this \
stochastic forcing the tensor grid needs its coordinates pinned explicitly \
(left to choose its own grid, the solver stalls), and pinning them to our own \
grid plus the duplicated endpoint has a bonus: the solver's samples land \
exactly on our grid points, so reading the state back involves no \
interpolation at all. Assemble the one call, taking the noise as any \
interpolated path; the potential enters as one pointwise factor, so any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " rides along. Two named options cover the two knobs later Parts will turn: \
the solver's step cap, by default a quarter of the path's knot spacing so no \
step straddles a knot, and a damping factor held at one, which exists so that \
the deliberately wrong It\[OHat] coefficient of Part IV will be literally one \
number in one call, not a retyped solver whose transcription would itself \
need auditing:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "smoothNoiseTrajectory", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Options", "[", "smoothNoiseTrajectory", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<StepCap\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<DampingFactor\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "g_", ",", " ", "vfun_", ",", " ", "lam_", ",", " ", "psi0_", ",", " ", 
     "tf_", ",", " ", "wf_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"OptionsPattern", "[", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "x", ",", " ", "t"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<n\>\"", "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<dx\>\"", "]"}], "/", "2."}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{"knot", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"wf", "[", "\"\<Coordinates\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"wf", "[", "\"\<Coordinates\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
         "     ", 
         RowBox[{"damp", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"OptionValue", "[", "\"\<DampingFactor\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"D", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"u", "[", 
               RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], 
            " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"I", " ", 
                RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
                 RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"D", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"u", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", 
             "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"I", "/", "hbar"}], ")"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"vfun", "[", "x", "]"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"u", "[", 
               RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
             RowBox[{"damp", " ", "lam", " ", 
              RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{"u", "[", 
               RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lam", "]"}], " ", "x", " ", 
              RowBox[{"u", "[", 
               RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"wf", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
           "      ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"u", "[", 
             RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{"psi0", "[", "x", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"u", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "a"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{"u", "[", 
             RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
         "     ", "u", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "tf"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "a"}], ",", " ", "a"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"MaxStepSize", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"If", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"OptionValue", "[", "\"\<StepCap\>\"", "]"}], " ", "===",
              " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"knot", "/", "4"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"OptionValue", "[", "\"\<StepCap\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",",
          "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<MethodOfLines\>\"", ",", " ", 
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<SpatialDiscretization\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", 
             "        ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"\"\<TensorProductGrid\>\"", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"\"\<Coordinates\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "a"}], 
                  "]"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "         ", 
               RowBox[{"\"\<DifferenceOrder\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "4"}]}], 
              "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[10]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The solution comes back as a function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 ", and we read it on our own grid: sampling at the grid points and \
multiplying by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 " lands the state in the parent essay's vector convention, except that its \
total weight now carries the likelihood instead of being pinned at one. \
Define the sampler and the weight:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sampleState", ",", " ", "norm2", ",", " ", "conditional"}], "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "sol_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<dx\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"sol", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"norm2", "[", "v_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "v", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "sol_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "sol", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[11]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every conditional quantity is then the parent's accessor applied to the \
normalized sample. Before any noise, hold the solver to the two evolutions we \
know exactly. With the measurement off, a free Gaussian of width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 " spreads so its position variance grows as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "0", "2"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["s", "TI"], "0"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 "; run it and compare the endpoint against that closed form, and the weight \
against one:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"128", ",", " ", "20."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "flat", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"flat", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0", " ", "x"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"s0F", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfF", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solFree", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "s0F"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", "tfF", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"tfF", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solFree", ",", " ", "tfF"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
     " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"s0F", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"hbar", " ", 
          RowBox[{"tfF", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "s0F"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], "^", 
        "2"}]}], ")"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"norm2", "[", 
      RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solFree", ",", " ", "tfF"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
     " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[12]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell["\<\
Both residuals are far below every effect we care about, and the first \
deserves to be split, because its two parts have different owners. The exact \
evolution on the ring costs one diagonal multiply in the momentum basis, with \
no solver at all; measure how far the solver's final variance sits from that \
exact ring propagation:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solFree", ",", " ", "tfF"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
   " ", "-", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
      RowBox[{"ift", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gF", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"tfF", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"ft", "[", 
         RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solFree", ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}], "]"}]}],
        "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[13]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The solver's own share is well over an order below the previous cell's \
residual: most of that residual belongs not to ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " but to the ring itself, the closed form describing an infinite line while \
the box folds the packet's spreading tails through the seam, exactly the \
effect ",
 Cell[BoxData["edgeMass"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 " is built to meter. So the floor under everything downstream has two \
layers, a solver layer far down and a topology layer the guards watch, and \
nothing later will need to resolve past either. (With the strength at zero \
the noise term is multiplied away, so the same call exercises the whole \
machinery.) Now the trap. A coherent state, the ground-state Gaussian \
displaced sideways, must swing rigidly, its center tracing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0"], 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 " with its width frozen at the ground-state value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "2", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 "; run one and read the worst deviation of both facts over the window:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"w0", " ", "=", " ", "0.8"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x0C", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "vHarm", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"vHarm", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0.5", " ", "mass", " ", 
    RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solCoh", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "0.", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x0C", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"2", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "w0"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "w0"}]}], ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "7"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solCoh", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
       "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"x0C", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
            RowBox[{"w0", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "w0"}]}], ",", " ", "40"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[14]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell["\<\
The center and the width both track the exact motion through a full period at \
the floor just priced, so the potential is wired correctly and the kinetic \
phases are resolved. This noise-off residual also identifies its owner. \
Fourth-order differences promise a specific reward for refining space, a \
sixteenfold drop per doubling of the grid; sweep the resolution on this same \
fixture and read the worst deviation at each. One adjustment as we do: the \
quarter-knot step cap exists to resolve the noise, and there is no noise \
here, so release it and let the adaptive error control own the step, which it \
already proved able to do on this fixture:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gN", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
          RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "20."}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"With", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
                RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"gN", ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                   "gN", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "0.", ",", "\n", 
                    "          ", 
                    RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"x0C", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
                    RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], 
                    "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "w0"}]}], ",", "\n", "          ", 
                    RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "w0"}]}], ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", 
                    "7"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"\"\<StepCap\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "0.1"}]}], 
                   "]"}], ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
              "       ", 
              RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"gN", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"x0C", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"w0", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"gN", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
                   RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}],
                "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
               RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "w0"}]}], ",", " ", "40"}], "]"}]}], 
             "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"128", ",", " ", "256", ",", " ", "512"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<worst deviation\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[15]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell["\<\
The first doubling collects nearly the full fourth-order reward; the second \
collects far less, the time integrator emerging as the new floor beneath the \
spatial one. So space owns this noise-off residual, and Part IV will show it \
owns almost none of the noisy one: three dials in this construction, each \
with its own jurisdiction. The machinery is certified quiet; time to switch \
the measurement on.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell["Part IV: One Trajectory: Held to Exact References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What makes the monitored particle such a sharp test bed is a classical fact \
about Gaussian states under quadratic Hamiltonians: the conditional state \
stays Gaussian, and its five moments close among themselves. Better still, \
the three covariances decouple from the noise entirely. Writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 " for the position variance, the symmetrized covariance, and the momentum \
variance, they obey the deterministic flow"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", "."], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "-", "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "2"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], "."], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
       StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
      SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", "."], 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "2"}], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{"4", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell["\<\
the same flow the parent essay solved for its steady state. Deterministic \
means pathwise: every single trajectory's width must ride this curve, \
whatever its noise does, which turns one run into an exact test with no \
ensemble in sight.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell["\<\
Two exact facts about this flow will serve as its credentials, so derive both \
before any integration. First the destination. At the fixed point all three \
rates vanish, three polynomial equations in three unknowns; solve them with \
every constant symbolic and keep the one branch a variance is allowed to \
occupy, the one that stays positive:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "sxS", ",", " ", "cS", ",", " ", "spS", ",", " ", "lamS", ",", " ", "mS", ",",
     " ", "hbS"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"steadyF", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SelectFirst", "[", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"SolveValues", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"cS", "/", "mS"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", 
             RowBox[{"sxS", "^", "2"}]}]}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"spS", "/", "mS"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", "sxS", " ", "cS"}]}], " ", "==", 
           " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"lamS", " ", 
             RowBox[{"hbS", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", 
             RowBox[{"cS", "^", "2"}]}]}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}], ",",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"sxS", ",", " ", "cS", ",", " ", "spS"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",",
       "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"TrueQ", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"lamS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"mS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"hbS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ",
        "&"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"lamS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"hbS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[16]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the correlation locks to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " regardless of the measurement strength, while the position variance \
narrows with the strength. Make that scaling a computation rather than a \
remark: rescale the strength by an arbitrary factor and read what happens to \
the steady width:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"steadyF", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lamS", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"a", " ", "lamS"}]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"steadyF", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"lamS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"hbS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"a", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[17]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Watching harder narrows the steady width only as the fourth root of the \
strength: information about position is expensive at the bottom. Two more \
facts should follow at once, the width formula the parent essay states, and a \
sharper one, that the steady triple saturates the \
Robertson-Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger floor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 ", because efficient monitoring keeps the state pure and a pure Gaussian \
sits exactly on that floor. Confirm both in one breath:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"steadyF", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"hbS", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", "mS"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "^", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"steadyF", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"steadyF", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"steadyF", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"hbS", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"lamS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"hbS", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both hold with every constant symbolic. Second, the whole road, not just \
its end: this flow is not merely integrable, it is solvable. Collect the \
covariances into the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["V", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " on the diagonal and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " off it, and the flow is a matrix Riccati equation, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "."], "=", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", 
   StyleBox["D", "TI"], "-", "4", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " the Hamilton drift, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 " the backaction heating, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " picking out the monitored entry. A Riccati flow linearizes by the oldest \
trick in filtering: write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 " and the pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],
 " obeys a linear system whose propagator is one matrix exponential, so"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThickSpace]", "=", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "11"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "12"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "21"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["M", "TI"], "22"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox[")",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["exp",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "(", GridBox[{
         {
          StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["D", "TI"]},
         {
          RowBox[{"4", 
           StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["E", "TI"]}], 
          RowBox[{"-", 
           SuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["T", "TI"]]}]}
        }], ")"}], "]"}], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell["\<\
Encode that closed form once, for any strength, trap frequency, and starting \
covariance:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "covFlow", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"covFlow", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lam_", ",", " ", "w_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"sx0_", ",", " ", "c0_", ",", " ", "sp0_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"aM", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"1", "/", "mass"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "mass"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"dM", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"lam", " ", 
             RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"eM", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"v0", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"sx0", ",", " ", "c0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"c0", ",", " ", "sp0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"m4", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", "\n", "        ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"ArrayFlatten", "[", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"aM", ",", " ", "dM"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"4", " ", "lam", " ", "eM"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"-", 
                   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "aM", "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], 
              "]"}], " ", "t"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"With", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"m4", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
                  " ", "v0"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"m4", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"3", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
               ")"}], " ", ".", "\n", "         ", 
              RowBox[{"Inverse", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"m4", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"3", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
                  " ", "v0"}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"m4", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"3", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"3", " ", ";;", " ", "4"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
               "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"v", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"v", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"v", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}],
         "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The closed form must own its credential, and the cheap way to certify a \
solution formula is not to chase its transcendental limits but to \
differentiate it. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " the pair starts at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "0"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "=", "\|01d7d9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 ", so the construction's derivative there is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], "0"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 " with both derivatives read straight off the linear system; that \
combination must equal the Riccati rate at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 ". Verify it as a polynomial matrix identity, the trap frequency and all \
three starting covariances fully symbolic:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sx0S", ",", " ", "c0S", ",", " ", "sp0S", ",", " ", "wS"}], "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"aM", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"1", "/", "mS"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "mS"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"wS", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"dM", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"lamS", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hbS", "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"eM", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"v0", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"sx0S", ",", " ", "c0S"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"c0S", ",", " ", "sp0S"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"aM", " ", ".", " ", "v0"}], " ", "+", " ", "dM"}], ")"}], 
      " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"v0", " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", 
          RowBox[{"eM", " ", ".", " ", "v0"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "aM", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], " ", "==", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"aM", " ", ".", " ", "v0"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"v0", " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "aM", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", "dM", " ", "-",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", 
       RowBox[{"v0", " ", ".", " ", "eM", " ", ".", " ", "v0"}]}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell["\<\
The identity holds for an arbitrary symmetric starting covariance, and that \
arbitrariness is what makes the local check global: the formula reproduces \
the Riccati rate from every starting point, so by uniqueness of the flow's \
solutions it is the solution, at all times, for any trap. Its long-time \
destination should then be the steady triple derived above; confirm that \
numerically at the fixture strength, late enough that the transient is long \
dead:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"covFlow", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"4.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "16."}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", "30.", "]"}], " ", 
    "-", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"steadyF", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"lamS", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mS", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"hbS", " ", "->", " ", "1."}]}], "}"}]}], ")"}]}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The flow lands on the derived triple. One limit more, because the steady \
algebra makes it free: let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 " and the steady conditional spread collapses entirely,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{"steadyF", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"hbS", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "so in the classical limit continuous measurement pins the particle exactly \
and the quantum filter becomes its classical Kalman ancestor: the residual \
width at finite ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[HBar]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 " is quantum mechanics refusing to be pinned. Now bind the exact flow at the \
fixture parameters of Part III's dispersion check (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 ", starting width ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1", "/", "16"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 " for a pure Gaussian):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ricF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"covFlow", "[", 
    RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"4.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "16."}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell["\<\
The referee is exact, so whatever daylight appears next belongs to the grid \
alone. Now run the monitored particle itself, the same seed-7 noise path as \
the dispersion check but with the measurement on, and overlay the \
trajectory's conditional width on the Riccati curve:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solM", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2.", ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2.", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solM", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ricF", "[", "tt", "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Automatic", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Placed", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<conditional width from the grid\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<deterministic Riccati flow\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      "Below"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<width\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<one noisy trajectory rides the noise-free width curve\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["\<\
The two curves lie on top of each other across the whole window: a state \
kicked by noise at every instant carries a width that never feels the noise, \
which is the Gaussian closure doing exactly what the algebra promised. Put a \
number on the overlay, the worst gap along the window:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solM", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
       "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ricF", "[", "tt", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "2.", ",", " ", "80"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell["\<\
The gap is thousands of times smaller than the width change it tracks: the \
smooth-noise route is integrating the measurement backaction, not merely \
surviving it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The width is one number; the conditional state carries a stronger \
credential, and the steady-state algebra above already named it. Under \
efficient monitoring a pure state stays pure, and for a Gaussian, purity is \
the single combination ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 ", pinned at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],
 ". That pinning is not a property of the steady state alone: substitute the \
three Riccati rates into the combination's own time derivative and it \
closes,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"]}], ")", "\[ThickSpace]", "=", "\[ThickSpace]",
     "4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "4"], "-", 
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
      StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], ")"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "so the purity floor is invariant and attracting at the rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 ", whatever the trap does. Verify that closure symbolically, trap frequency \
included:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sxD", ",", " ", "cD", ",", " ", "spD", ",", " ", "wD"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"spD", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cD", "/", "mS"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", 
       RowBox[{"sxD", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"sxD", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "mS", " ", 
       RowBox[{"wD", "^", "2"}], " ", "cD"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lamS", " ", 
       RowBox[{"hbS", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cD", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"2", " ", "cD", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"spD", "/", "mS"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mS", " ", 
       RowBox[{"wD", "^", "2"}], " ", "sxD"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", "sxD", " ", "cD"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"4", " ", "lamS", " ", "sxD", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"hbS", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"sxD", " ", "spD"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"cD", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The rate closes identically, with the trap frequency cancelling on its own: \
the trap turns the state in phase space but never moves it off the purity \
shell. Now hold the grid to the whole covariance triple at once, not just the \
width: read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 " off the seed-7 state at the final time, the momentum pieces through the \
transform pair, and set each beside the Riccati flow's value:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"covTriple", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solM", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"fv", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ft", "[", "v", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"xm", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"pm", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"gF", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "fv", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
         "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "v", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"gF", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", 
                RowBox[{"ift", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"gF", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], " ", "fv"}], "]"}]}],
                ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"xm", " ", "pm"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"gF", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", 
             " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "fv", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"pm", "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<\[CapitalSigma]x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<C\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<\[CapitalSigma]p\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"covTriple", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ricF", "[", "2.", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All three components sit at the same scale as the width alone did, so the \
backaction heating in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " and the cross correlation in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],
 " are integrated as faithfully as the narrowing in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 ". And now the purity credential:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"covTriple", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"covTriple", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"covTriple", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], "/", "4"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell["\<\
The grid state sits on the purity shell several orders more tightly than any \
single component matches the Riccati flow: the solver's errors slide the \
covariance triple along the shell rather than off it, which is exactly what \
the attracting closure above demands of a small perturbation. A wrong \
diffusion coefficient could not hide here; it would push the triple off the \
shell at the rate the closure names.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That was the invariant half of the Gaussian closure. The driven half is \
sharper still. The conditional means follow the noise, but through a specific \
filter: writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " for the innovation (what remains of the record after subtracting the \
signal the current estimate predicts), ordinary calculus on the smooth flow \
gives"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "+", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SqrtBox[
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Nu]", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell["\<\
with the covariance block feeding the gains, and the covariance block is the \
exact flow we already hold in closed form, so only the two means actually \
need integrating. Here is the point that makes this an exact test rather than \
a limit statement: for the smooth noise these moment equations hold at any \
drawing step, because the closure is algebra, not stochastic calculus. So the \
wavefunction on its 128-point grid and a driven pair of means riding exact \
gains, fed by the same interpolated path, must produce the same conditional \
mean, and the residual between them is pure solver error with no \
noise-resolution floor underneath. Run both in a harmonic trap from a \
displaced start, a fresh seed, the small system integrated tightly since it \
referees, and read the worst disagreement in the mean position:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lamT", " ", "=", " ", "0.6"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"sT", " ", "=", " ", "1.2"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"x0T", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"wfM", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
    RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "13"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "lamT", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x0T", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "sT"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1.", 
     ",", " ", "wfM"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"covT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"covFlow", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lamT", ",", " ", "w0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sT", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", 
          RowBox[{"sT", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "covTN", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"covTN", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"tt_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", "k_Integer"}], "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"covT", "[", "tt", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "k", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"momT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"mx", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"mp", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mass"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lamT", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"covTN", "[", 
           RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"wfM", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lamT", "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"mx", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"mp", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "mass"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"w0", "^", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"mx", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lamT", "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"covTN", "[", 
           RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"wfM", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lamT", "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"mx", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"mx", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "x0T"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"mp", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0."}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", "mx", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"MaxStepSize", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0.005", "/", "16"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"AccuracyGoal", " ", "->", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PrecisionGoal", " ", "->", " ", "10"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "worstMeanGap", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"worstMeanGap", "[", "sol_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "sol", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
        " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"momT", "[", "tt", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "80"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"worstMeanGap", "[", "solT", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[29]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The grid's complex amplitudes against a driven pair of means, and the two \
integrators agree on the conditional mean to a small fraction of its swing. \
This is the continuous-space sibling of the qubit essay's closed record \
identity: an exact pathwise consequence of the equations that any correct \
integrator must honor at its own precision, with nothing waiting on the \
white-noise limit. And because the identity is exact, its residual must be \
bought down by solver effort alone. The dial that matters is the one Part III \
flagged: how finely the solver chops the jagged forcing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[Prime]"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 ". Hold the grid and the noise fixed, cap the wavefunction solver's steps \
four times finer through the call's step-cap option, and watch the residual \
fall:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"worstMeanGap", "[", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "lamT", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"x0T", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "sT"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1.", 
     ",", " ", "wfM", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<StepCap\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0.005", "/", "16"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/", " ", 
  RowBox[{"worstMeanGap", "[", "solT", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[30]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],

Cell["\<\
The residual falls severalfold with nothing changed but the step cap, \
confirming its reading as integration error and nothing else: the identity \
itself is exact at this noise resolution, so only the solvers stand between \
the two curves, with the residual tracking the cap nearly in proportion.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One certification remains, and it is the one that bites: falsifiability. \
Everything above would deserve no trust if it also passed with the wrong \
equation. The wrong equation is one coefficient away, the It\[OHat] damping \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " fed to a solver that integrates smoothly, and the assembled call's damping \
multiplier makes it exactly one number in one call, with every other byte of \
the discretization shared. Run it on the same seed-7 fixture as the width \
test, and read both drifts' endpoint width against the Riccati reference:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solWrong", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2.", ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2.", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<DampingFactor\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<\[Lambda]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Lambda]/2\>\""}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solM", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
        "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ricF", "[", "2.", "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solWrong", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}]}], 
         "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ricF", "[", "2.", "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[31]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell["\<\
The It\[OHat] damping misses the reference by three orders of magnitude more \
than the Stratonovich damping, a gap no solver tolerance can produce. In \
other words, the comparison is genuinely able to fail, and the doubled \
damping is what makes it pass: the factor of two from Part II is \
load-bearing, and the machinery would have caught us had we dropped it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell["\<\
There is one more dial to interrogate, and here this essay parts company with \
its qubit sibling. Two time steps live in the construction: the noise-drawing \
step, which fixes the physics, and the solver's step cap, which should carry \
none. For the qubit, relaxing the cap moved nothing; here the forcing wiggles \
on a 128-point grid's fastest scales, and the cap earns its keep. Rerun the \
fixture with the cap relaxed from a quarter of the knot spacing to the full \
knot spacing, and read the width's distance from the Riccati reference:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
     RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
           RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
          "       ", "2.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2.", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<StepCap\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "0.005"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
        " ", "2."}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ricF", "[", "2.", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[32]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],

Cell["\<\
The distance is small but resolvable, well over an order of magnitude above \
the pinned-cap residual: unlike the qubit case, the adaptive error control \
alone does not fully resolve this forcing, so the quarter-knot cap is not a \
ritual here but a working part. And the third dial, the one that owned Part \
III's noise-off floor, owns almost nothing here: double the spatial grid \
under the same noise and cap, and read the monitored width's whole-window \
distance from the exact flow:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"g2", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
      RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "20."}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
          RowBox[{"g2", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
            RowBox[{"g2", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
              RowBox[{
              "g2", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "1.", ",", "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
                RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "s0F"}], "]"}], ",", 
               " ", "tfF", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
                RowBox[{"tfF", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "7"}], "]"}]}], 
              "]"}], ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", 
        "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ricF", "[", "tt", "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tfF", ",", " ", "80"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[33]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell["\<\
The distance barely moves from its 128-point value: the monitored residual \
belongs to the cap and the drawing step, not to space. All three dials now \
have measured owners, space holding the noise-off floor, the cap holding a \
visible slice at fixed noise, and the drawing step holding which stochastic \
equation is being solved, which is the ensemble statement Part V closes with.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell["Part V: The Ensemble: What Needs Weights and What Does Not", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A single record shows the filter working; the statistics live across \
records. Part I proved two ensemble facts symbolically: averages of \
quantities linear in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " need no likelihood weight, and the weight itself averages to one. Both are \
now one ensemble away from being watched. Launch the parallel kernels and \
share the definitions the trajectories need:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"LaunchKernels", "[", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"DistributeDefinitions", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "hbar", ",", " ", "mass", ",", " ", "grid", ",", " ", "wienerPath", ",", 
    " ", "smoothNoiseTrajectory", ",", "\n", "  ", "sampleState", ",", " ", 
    "norm2", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "packet"}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[34]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell["\<\
Fix the ensemble study: a free particle at moderate strength from a narrow \
packet, a short window, and a few hundred trajectories, each read off at the \
final time as a raw, unnormalized sample vector:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"128", ",", " ", "20."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"lamE", " ", "=", " ", "0.5"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"tfE", " ", "=", " ", "0.75"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ntraj", " ", "=", " ", "400"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ensembleE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ParallelTable", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gE", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gE", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "lamE", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
         "     ", "tfE", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
          RowBox[{"tfE", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"3000", " ", "+", " ", "k"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       "tfE"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntraj"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[35]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First the alarm bell. Each raw sample carries its likelihood ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {GridBox[{
        {
         TemplateBox[{
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
          "Ket"]}
       },
       GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
       GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 ", and Part I's trace identity says the ensemble mean of that weight is \
pinned at one for all time; a wrong drift, by contrast, sends it off \
exponentially, which makes this single number the cheapest wiring check the \
construction owns. Read the mean weight's distance from one in units of its \
own standard error:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"weightsE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "ensembleE", "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "weightsE", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "/", 
  
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "weightsE", "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "ntraj", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[36]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The mean weight sits within ordinary sampling scatter of one, so the drift, \
the diffusion, and their Stratonovich bookkeeping are consistent across the \
whole ensemble, not merely on the fixtures of Part IV. The weights are \
legitimately spread out, though, and their spread measures how unequally the \
records share the ensemble's statistical work. The standard summary is the \
ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["w", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 ", which counts how many equally-weighted trajectories the weighted ensemble \
is effectively worth (the effective sample size of importance sampling); read \
it beside the raw count:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"ntraj", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", "weightsE", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{"weightsE", "^", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[37]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell["\<\
The weighting spends a real share of the nominal count at this strength and \
horizon, and what survives is what funds the error bars of every weighted \
estimate below; push the horizon out and the surviving fraction falls, which \
is the practical boundary of the reference-measure ensemble, and Part VIII \
returns to it with a longer run.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the Lindblad fact. The unconditional second moments obey the closed \
chain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", "."], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["u", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["u", "TI"]], "/", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["C", "TI"], "."], 
    StyleBox["u", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["u", "TI"]], "/", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", "."], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["u", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 " for the free particle: measurement heats the momentum at the constant rate \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 ", the parent essay's backaction fact, and two integrations pass the heat \
into position. Solve the chain exactly, every constant symbolic, so the \
structure shows itself rather than being asserted:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "uncondSym", ",", " ", "lamU", ",", " ", "sx0U", ",", " ", "sp0U"}], "]"}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"uncondSym", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"DSolveValue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"sxu", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cu", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mS"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"cu", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"spu", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "mS"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"spu", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"lamU", " ", 
         RowBox[{"hbS", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"sxu", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "sx0U"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"cu", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"spu", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "sp0U"}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sxu", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"spu", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[38]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

Cell["\<\
There is the whole story in two lines: momentum takes the heat linearly, and \
position receives it as the cubic term riding on the free ballistic \
spreading, the momentum random walk integrated twice. Bind the chain at the \
ensemble's parameters, keeping both numbers for the cells below:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"uncondSx", ",", " ", "uncondSp"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"uncondSym", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"mS", " ", "->", " ", "mass"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"hbS", " ", "->", " ", "hbar"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lamU", " ", "->", " ", "lamE"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"sx0U", " ", "->", " ", "1."}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"sp0U", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], "/", "4."}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"t", " ", "->", " ", "tfE"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<\[CapitalSigma]x\>\"", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<\[CapitalSigma]p\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"uncondSx", ",", " ", "uncondSp"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[39]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Note where the heating's share sits: over this short window it is the \
majority of the momentum moment but only a sliver of the position one, so the \
momentum is where a wrong heating rate would stand convicted, while the \
position mostly certifies the free flow the heat rides on. The grid ensemble \
must reproduce both numbers through nothing but raw quadratic forms: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 " is linear in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],
 ", so averaging ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Bra"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 " with no weights and no normalization must land on it. Read the position \
moment's standardized gap:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x2raw", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "ensembleE", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gE", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "x2raw", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "uncondSx"}], "]"}], "/", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "x2raw", "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "ntraj", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[40]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell["\<\
The unweighted average of an unnormalized quadratic form lands on the exact \
Lindblad moment within sampling scatter: the likelihood weight really does \
live inside the raw state, which is the cleanest statement of why linear \
observables are weight-free. The sharp half of the claim is the momentum's. \
Rotate each raw sample to the momentum basis with the transform pair, where \
the same quadratic form is again a plain dot product, and read that moment's \
standardized gap:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"p2raw", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"ft", " ", "/@", " ", "ensembleE"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gE", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "p2raw", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "uncondSp"}], "]"}], "/", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "p2raw", "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "ntraj", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[41]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell["\<\
The momentum moment, where the backaction heating is the dominant share, \
lands within sampling scatter too: the ensemble certifies the heating rate \
itself, not merely the free flow it rides on, and this is the cell that earns \
the phrase \"rebuilds the Lindblad master equation\".\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell["\<\
Where the weight earns its keep is one nonlinearity away. Ask instead for the \
spread of the conditional mean position across records, a quantity quadratic \
in the normalized state. The law of total variance fixes its exact value: the \
unconditional variance splits into the width every conditional state shares \
(the deterministic Riccati value) plus the variance of where those \
conditional states sit,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Var",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox[")",
     FontSize->1.2 Inherited], "\[ThickSpace]", "=", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["u", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThickSpace]", "-", "\[ThickSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],

Cell["\<\
both terms already in hand. Compute the target from the two references, and \
the conditional means, each raw first moment divided by its own weight:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ricE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"covFlow", "[", 
    RowBox[{"lamE", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"hbar", "^", "2"}], "/", "4."}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"targetVar", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"uncondSx", " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ricE", "[", "tfE", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mxE", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "ensembleE", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gE", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "weightsE"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[42]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],

Cell["\<\
An estimate deserves an error bar, and this estimator's is priced the way \
every neighboring cell's was, by its own scatter: resample the four hundred \
trajectories with replacement, recompute the estimate on each resample, and \
the spread of those recomputations is the estimator's standard error. Define \
that yardstick once, for any estimator built on trajectory indices, then read \
the weighted estimate's gap from the target in its own standard errors:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"spreadGapSE", ",", " ", "wSpread"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"spreadGapSE", "[", "est_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "77", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"est", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", "ntraj", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        "targetVar"}], "]"}], "/", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"est", "[", 
          RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Range", "[", "ntraj", "]"}], ",", " ", "ntraj"}], "]"}], 
          "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "800", "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wSpread", "[", "idx_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"weightsE", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "idx", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
         RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
          RowBox[{"weightsE", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "idx", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mxE", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "idx", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
       RowBox[{"w", " ", 
        RowBox[{"m", "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
        RowBox[{"w", " ", "m"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"spreadGapSE", "[", "wSpread", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[43]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell["\<\
The weighted estimate lands on the law-of-total-variance target within one of \
its own standard errors. Now remove the weights and put the same yardstick on \
the same estimator:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "uSpread", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"uSpread", "[", "idx_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"mxE", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "idx", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", "^", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "m", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"spreadGapSE", "[", "uSpread", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[44]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell["\<\
The unweighted spread misses the target by tens of its own standard errors: \
without its likelihood, each record testifies with the wrong voice, and the \
ensemble votes itself away from the physical measure, decisively. This pair \
of cells is the measure bookkeeping of Part I made operational: linear \
observables free, nonlinear conditional statistics weighted, nothing in \
between.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],

Cell["\<\
Last, the promised sweep of the one physics dial. The drawing step of the \
noise fixes which stochastic equation the smooth forcing represents, so \
coarsening it should move the ensemble's physics while refining it should \
not; the Lindblad moment just computed is the natural meter. But comparing \
two independently drawn ensembles would squander the question in their \
unshared randomness. Instead, coarsen the very same paths: keep every fifth \
knot of each trajectory's own Wiener path, reinterpolate, rerun, and read the \
paired difference of the position moment, trajectory by trajectory, in units \
of its own standard error, so that everything the two runs share cancels and \
only the smoothing bias remains:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "coarsen", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coarsen", "[", 
    RowBox[{"wf_", ",", " ", "k_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"kn", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"wf", "[", "\"\<Coordinates\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Interpolation", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"kn", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "k"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"wf", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"kn", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "k"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], 
         "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"InterpolationOrder", " ", "->", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"coarsePaths", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"coarsen", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
        RowBox[{"tfE", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"3000", " ", "+", " ", "k"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "5"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntraj"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ensembleC", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ParallelTable", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gE", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gE", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "lamE", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         "tfE", ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"coarsePaths", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "k", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "tfE"}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntraj"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"x2rawC", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "ensembleC", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gE", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x2rawC", " ", "-", " ", "x2raw"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", 
     RowBox[{"x2rawC", " ", "-", " ", "x2raw"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "ntraj", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[45]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell["\<\
The paired difference sits within ordinary scatter of zero, and the pairing \
is what gives that verdict its weight: with the shared randomness cancelled, \
this comparison resolves smoothing bias many times finer than two independent \
ensembles could, and still finds none at a fivefold coarser draw. At this \
strength the working step carries real margin, exactly the situation the \
qubit essay found for its mean; the dial is real, but it is already turned \
far enough.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell["\<\
Part VI: Filtering Across Engines: One Record, Two Integrators, One State\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell["\<\
Part I called the linear equation a filter: feed it a record, and it produces \
the conditional state consistent with that record. So far every record we fed \
it was a plain Wiener path standing in for the raw detector output. The claim \
has a far stronger form: feed it a record produced by a different integrator \
built on different mathematics, and it must reconstruct that integrator's \
conditional state, pathwise, with no ensemble to hide in. The parent essay's \
engine is exactly such a stranger: it never sees a stochastic differential \
equation, advancing instead by an exact Bayesian reweighting followed by a \
split-step Fourier drift. One record, two unrelated machines, one state: that \
is the test.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell["\<\
Port the parent engine in its two moves, the Gaussian-likelihood measurement \
update and the symmetric split drift:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"measUpdate", ",", " ", "evolveStep", ",", " ", "stepV"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "lam_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "xb_"}], 
     "]"}], "[", "psi_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "lam"}], " ", "dt", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xb"}], ")"}], 
        "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "psi"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"evolveStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "vfun_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"kin", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"pot", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"vfun", "[", 
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"psi", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"pot", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ift", "[", 
         RowBox[{"kin", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ft", "[", 
           RowBox[{"pot", " ", "psi"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "vfun_", ",", " ", "lam_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], 
     "]"}], "[", "psi_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"xb", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "psi", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", 
        "     ", 
        RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
         RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"4", " ", "lam", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"evolveStep", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "lam", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "xb"}], 
          "]"}], "[", "psi", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "xb"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[46]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run the engine in the harmonic trap from the ground state, keeping the \
conditional state and the outcome at every step; each outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],
 " is the record increment in position units, so the running record is their \
weighted cumulative sum, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dtK", " ", "=", " ", "0.01"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ntK", " ", "=", " ", "100"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"lamK", " ", "=", " ", "0.6"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"statesK", ",", " ", "outsK"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "21", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Rest", "[", 
       RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "gF", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "lamK", ",", " ", "dtK"}], 
            "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"First", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
         "      ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", "ntK", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"recordY", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Interpolation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"dtK", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "ntK"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lamK", "]"}], " ", "dtK", " ", "outsK"}], 
           "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InterpolationOrder", " ", "->", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[47]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the filtering step, and notice that nothing about ",
 Cell[BoxData["smoothNoiseTrajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 " changes: the record path enters exactly where the Wiener path did, because \
the linear equation never knew the difference; that indifference is the \
filter property. The one bookkeeping point is the smoothing correction: the \
record's fluctuating part is the same Wiener noise, so its quadratic \
variation is the same, and the doubled damping of Part II carries over \
unchanged. Drive the equation with the interpolated record from the same \
initial state:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solK", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "lamK", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"dtK", " ", "ntK"}], ",", " ", "recordY"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[48]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],

Cell["\<\
The two engines now hold rival conditional states at every step. Compare them \
where a state comparison is sharpest, the overlap: read the worst infidelity, \
one minus the squared overlap between the normalized grid samples, over the \
full window:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solK", ",", " ", "#1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
         " ", ".", " ", "#2"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"dtK", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "ntK", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "statesK"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[49]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell["\<\
The infidelity stays small along the whole record: two integrators that share \
not one line of numerics, one advancing by Bayes' rule and Fourier \
transforms, the other by a finite-difference method of lines on a smoothed \
record, agree on the conditional state to high fidelity at every step. What \
residual remains is the discretization mismatch between a step-wise record \
and its smooth interpolant, so it must shrink when the record is cut finer, \
with one proviso Part IV taught us to expect: a finer record has a wilder \
interpolant, so the filter must also be allowed proportionally finer steps, \
or its own integration error takes over the comparison. Cut the engine's step \
five times finer, rebuild the record, refilter with the cap tightened through \
the call's step-cap option, and read the same worst infidelity:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"statesK2", ",", " ", "outsK2"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "22", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Rest", "[", 
       RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "gF", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "lamK", ",", " ", "0.002"}], 
            "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"First", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
         "      ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", "500", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"recordY2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Interpolation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0.002", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "500"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "lamK", "]"}], " ", "0.002", " ", "outsK2"}],
            "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InterpolationOrder", " ", "->", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solK2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "vHarm", ",", " ", "lamK", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
        RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "w0"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", "1.", ",", " ", "recordY2", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<StepCap\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"0.002", "/", "16"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "solK2", ",", " ", "#1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
         " ", ".", " ", "#2"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0.002", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "500", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "statesK2"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[50]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell["\<\
The infidelity falls by more than an order of magnitude below even the coarse \
record's value, confirming the reading: the residual is the conditioning \
mismatch of a step-wise record against its smooth stand-in, it shrinks with \
the record's step once the filter is allowed to resolve the finer \
interpolant, and nowhere in it is there a disagreement about the physics. \
This closes the loop the two essays share: the parent built the conditional \
state from Bayes' rule, the qubit companion built state and record from one \
stochastic equation, and here a record from the first construction drives the \
second and lands on the same state. Filtering is not a metaphor for what the \
linear equation does; it is the computation, and two unrelated engines just \
performed it on the same data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell["\<\
Part VII: Leaving the Quadratic Nest: a Double Well and a Cat\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every state so far was a Gaussian in a quadratic potential, which is \
precisely where closed-form referees exist, and precisely what the \
construction never assumed. The potential entered ",
 Cell[BoxData["smoothNoiseTrajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 " as one pointwise factor, so trading the trap for a double well costs one \
definition, and it buys the regime the closing claim is about: a state with \
two peaks, a potential with two valleys, and no five-moment closure anywhere \
to check against. What stays on duty are the model-free instruments, the \
guards, and they are about to be needed for real work."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Fix a quartic with valleys at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],
 " and start the particle as a cat, one lobe resting in each valley, built \
from the same packet helper:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gW", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "20."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"vWell", ",", " ", "catWell"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"vWell", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"0.02", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "9."}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"catWell", "[", "x_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "3."}], ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.8"}], "]"}], "[", 
       "x", "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
        RowBox[{"3.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.8"}], "]"}], "[", "x", 
       "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solW", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "gW", ",", " ", "vWell", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "catWell", ",", " ", 
     "1.5", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1.5", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "29"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[51]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],

Cell["\<\
First certify that this really is the regime the closures cannot reach. A \
Gaussian's fourth central moment is locked to its second (three times its \
square), so the excess kurtosis, the fourth central moment over the squared \
second minus that Gaussian three, measures the departure, and a two-lobed \
density drives it far negative. Read it at the start and at the end of the \
run:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "excessKurtosis", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"excessKurtosis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "v", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xm", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xm"}], ")"}],
          "^", "4"}], " ", ".", " ", "p"}], "/", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xm"}], 
            ")"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", "p"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ",
       "-", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"excessKurtosis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", "solW", ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"excessKurtosis", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", "solW", ",", " ", "1.5"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[52]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],

Cell["\<\
The start sits far below the Gaussian benchmark, as a two-lobed state must, \
and the endpoint has climbed back toward it: something destroyed the \
two-lobed structure along the way. Watch it happen through the probability of \
finding the particle right of center:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "rightMass", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rightMass", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Pick", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "v", "]"}], "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"rightMass", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
          RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", "solW", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
        RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1.5", ",", " ", "60"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<probability right of center\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<continuous measurement decides the valley\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[53]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The curve leaves even odds and pins to a definite verdict: the double-well \
cat collapses into a single valley under nothing but continuous position \
measurement, the continuous-space twin of the parent essay's two-packet \
collapse, now with a potential shaping the lobes while it happens. Which \
valley wins belongs to this record's noise; a different seed decides \
differently. No closed form referees this regime, but Part VI's other engine \
does, because nothing in the Bayes/split-step construction was quadratic \
either. Generate a double-well record with that engine from the same cat, \
filter it through the same ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],
 " call, and read the worst infidelity between the two engines' conditional \
states along the run:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"statesW", ",", " ", "outsW"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "31", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Rest", "[", 
       RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "gW", ",", " ", "vWell", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "0.005"}], 
            "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"First", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
         "      ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gW", "[", "\"\<dx\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"catWell", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gW", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ",
            "0."}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", "300", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"recordW", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Interpolation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"0.005", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "300"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "0.5", "]"}], " ", "0.005", " ", "outsW"}], 
           "]"}], ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"InterpolationOrder", " ", "->", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solWF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "gW", ",", " ", "vWell", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "catWell", ",", " ", 
     "1.5", ",", " ", "recordW"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", "solWF", ",", " ", "#1"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
         " ", ".", " ", "#2"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0.005", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "300", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "statesW"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[54]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],

Cell["\<\
Two unrelated integrators, one double-well record, one conditional state to \
high fidelity: the collapse above is engine-independent, and the cross-engine \
certification of Part VI survives the crossing out of the quadratic nest. The \
run also carried its instruments; read both guards over the whole window:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"edgeMass", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", "solW", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1.5", ",", " ", "30"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"tailMass", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gW", ",", " ", "solW", ",", " ", "tt"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tt", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "1.5", ",", " ", "30"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[55]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],

Cell["\<\
Both leakages stay negligible, so the verdict above is the continuum's, not \
an artifact of the box: model-free instruments are exactly what survives the \
crossing out of the quadratic nest.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell["Part VIII: Guards, and What Is Now True", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell["\<\
Every quantitative claim above lives on a finite grid, and the parent essay's \
discipline applies unchanged: the grid is faithful only while the packet \
keeps clear of the box seam and the top of the momentum ladder. The guards \
are already defined, so point them at the stored ensemble of Part V, \
normalizing each sample first so the guard reads a fraction of the state's \
own weight. Read the worst position leakage over all trajectories:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"edgeMass", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gE", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
    "ensembleE"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[56]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],

Cell["\<\
Then the worst momentum leakage, the share that ever reached the fastest \
tenth of the ladder:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"tailMass", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gE", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
    "ensembleE"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[57]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],

Cell["\<\
Both leakages stay negligible across all trajectories: nothing in Part V ever \
felt the seam or the ladder, so the ensemble numbers stand. A guard that \
never fires is indistinguishable from a guard wired to nothing, so fire it on \
purpose: launch a fast packet from the middle of a small box with the \
measurement off, so it coasts into the seam region, and read the same \
position guard at the moment it arrives:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gS", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "10."}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"solSeam", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "4.", ",", " ", "0.5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1.2",
      ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1.2", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"edgeMass", "[", 
  RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "solSeam", ",", " ", "1.2"}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[58]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],

Cell["\<\
The guard reads an order-one fraction where the ensemble's runs read \
essentially zero: it was armed all along, and its silence in Part V was \
earned, not decorative. A run that exercises the seam is also exactly where \
the boundary condition itself should be certified, so hold this one to the \
two invariants the interior runs enjoyed, the norm and, the measurement being \
off, the exact ring propagation:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"norm2", "[", 
      RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "solSeam", ",", " ", "1.2"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
     " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"conditional", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "solSeam", ",", " ", "1.2"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
       " ", ".", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
        RowBox[{"ift", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"gS", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
            RowBox[{"1.2", "/", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
          
          RowBox[{"ft", "[", 
           RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
            RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", "solSeam", ",", " ", "0."}], "]"}], 
           "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[59]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],

Cell["\<\
Crossing the seam costs the raw norm noticeably more than the interior runs \
ever paid, yet the normalized state still lies on the exact ring evolution at \
the interior floor: the seam leaks a little amplitude, not physics, and every \
conditional readout in this document is renormalized and therefore immune to \
that leak. One more finite resource deserves the same treatment: the \
likelihood itself. The weight spread of Part V grows with the horizon, \
eroding the surviving count that funds every weighted error bar. Measure the \
erosion rather than asserting it: quadruple Part V's horizon at the same \
strength, same nominal count, and read the surviving count again:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"weightsLong", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ParallelTable", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
        RowBox[{"sampleState", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gE", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"smoothNoiseTrajectory", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "gE", ",", " ", "flat", ",", " ", "lamE", ",", "\n", "       ", 
            RowBox[{"packet", "[", 
             RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "1."}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            "3.", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"wienerPath", "[", 
             RowBox[{"3.", ",", " ", "0.005", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"7000", " ", "+", " ", "k"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
          " ", "3."}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "ntraj"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"ntraj", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Total", "[", "weightsLong", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{"weightsLong", "^", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[60]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],

Cell["\<\
The surviving fraction falls further below its short-horizon value, and the \
mechanism is worth naming, because it also says why the fall is gradual \
rather than a cliff here: the weights spread while the records still disagree \
about where the particle is, and once the measurement has localized it, each \
record's information rate levels off, so the erosion accumulates rather than \
explodes. Still, the direction only goes one way: longer horizons pay ever \
more trajectories for ever fewer effective ones, and that economics, not any \
solver failure, is the practical boundary of driving the linear equation with \
plain Wiener paths. Past it, one generates records the physical way, as Part \
VI did, and filters those instead.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here is the summary. The physical measurement equation is nonlocal in \
exactly the coefficient a spatial discretizer must sample, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],
 " cannot hold it; the linear, unnormalized form has pointwise coefficients, \
and the norm it sheds is the likelihood of the record, so nothing physical is \
lost, only relocated. Handing that linear equation to ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 " takes one change of calculus, the damping doubled from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],
 " because a smooth noise integrates in the Stratonovich sense, and one \
discretization decision, the tensor-product grid pinned to our own points \
with periodicity stated as an equation. So certified, the route is exact \
where the mathematics is exact: the conditional covariances ride the \
closed-form Riccati flow pathwise and stay pinned to the purity shell, the \
conditional means agree with a driven pair riding that flow's exact gains \
down to solver error at any noise resolution, and the wrong calculus misses \
by orders of magnitude. Ensembles need no weights for anything linear in the \
density matrix, where the raw quadratic forms rebuild the Lindblad master \
equation, and need exactly the squared norms for anything nonlinear, where \
they land the spread of the conditional mean on the law of total variance. \
And because the equation is a filter, the same call that consumed synthetic \
Wiener paths consumes a record made by the parent essay's Bayesian engine and \
reconstructs that engine's conditional state pathwise. What the construction \
buys, beyond the qubit companion's lesson, is reach: the potential enters as \
one pointwise factor, and Part VII spent that freedom where no five-moment \
closure exists, watching continuous measurement collapse a double-well cat \
into a single valley with only the model-free guards on duty, which is \
precisely the regime a certified integrator is for."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"]
},
